    "title": "Detect Cycle in a Directed Graph",
    "category": "Graphs",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "problemStatement": "Given a directed graph with N vertices and M directed edges, determine whether the graph contains at least one cycle.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains two integers N and M. \u2022 The next M lines each contain two integers u and v, representing a directed edge from u to v.",
    "output": "Print YES if the graph contains a cycle; otherwise print NO.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 10^5 \u2022 0 \u2264 M \u2264 2\u00d710^5 \u2022 1 \u2264 u, v \u2264 N"
